      {
        "round": 1,
        "agent": "supplier_1",
        "kind": "message",
        "text": "PLANNING ROUND 1 \u2014 STRATEGY ANALYSIS\n\nMy cost: 21 credits/part. I want to maximize total profit across the game.\n\nKey insight: If I price P1 and I'm the cheapest supplier, my profit per unit = (P1 - 21), and quantity Q = (120 - P1)/2 (optimal retail price R = (120+P1)/2 maximizes manufacturer profit).\n\nProfit function: f(P1) = (P1-21) * (120-P1)/2\n\nThis is a concave parabola. Maximum at P1 = 70.5, giving f(70)=f(71)=1225.\n\nRisks:\n- If supplier_2 undercuts P1, I supply 0.\n- If both tie, I get half the quantity.\n\nStrategy: I will post P1 around 70-71 (to balance margin and quantity). I'll post a high-enough price to ensure competitiveness but not so high that I'm guaranteed to be cheapest only if supplier_2 is also high.\n\nSince I can't know supplier_2's price, I'll start by posting an intended price and testing responses."
      },
      {
        "round": 2,
        "agent": "supplier_2",
        "kind": "message",
        "text": "Cost: 22 credits/part. I will aim to undercut supplier_1 if possible to secure the full quantity, as the manufacturer's retail price is determined by the minimum input price. I will post a price to ensure competitiveness."
      },
      {
        "round": 2,
        "agent": "supplier_2",
        "kind": "message",
        "text": "My intent: Given supplier_1 posted 71, I'm posting 68 as a test. This is below supplier_1's price, so I'm the cheapest supplier and will supply all units (manufacturer takes from me). I expect manufacturer to likely match their previous pattern with a retail price near 95-96."
      },
      {
        "round": 3,
        "agent": "supplier_1",
        "kind": "message",
        "text": "Round 3 planning note: Cost=21. I posted P1=71 as a test. The key decision hinges on supplier_2's response. If they post above 71, I'm cheapest and get Q=(120-71)/2=49.5 units at profit 50/unit = ~2475. If they post below 71, they win and I earn 0. Last period their best was 68 (Q=26). Expect them to be near 68-71 range. Monitor execution results."
      },
      {
        "round": 6,
        "agent": "supplier_2",
        "kind": "message",
        "text": "PLANNING ROUND 6: I will post P2=70. This keeps me competitive with supplier_1's 69-71 range while maximizing profit among cheapest-competitive prices. If supplier_1 posts 71 or higher, I'll still be cheapest or tied. I expect manufacturer to price around 95-96 (optimal R=(120+70)/2=95)."
      },
      {
        "round": 8,
